WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.397
Marilla put her knitting on her lap. Her eyes were tired again.

2
00:00:07.398 --> 00:00:13.160
Anne was curled up on the rug in front of the fire. Marilla looked at her with tenderness.

3
00:00:13.161 --> 00:00:16.652
Anne had no idea of how much Marilla loved her.

4
00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:20.985
Anne sometimes thought Marilla was hard to please and lacked understanding.

5
00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:25.799
But she always stopped that thought and remembered what she owed to Marilla.

6
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.667
"Anne," Marilla said abruptly, "Miss Stacy was here this afternoon."

7
00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:33.735
"Was she? Why?" asked Anne.

8
00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:36.970
"She came to talk about you," answered Marilla.

9
00:00:36.971 --> 00:00:44.058
"About me?" Anne looked rather scared. Then she flushed and exclaimed, "Oh, I know what she said.

10
00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:48.391
I meant to tell you, Marilla, honestly I did, but I forgot.

11
00:00:48.392 --> 00:00:55.604
Miss Stacy caught me reading Ben-Hur in school when I should have been studying Canadian history.

12
00:00:55.605 --> 00:01:00.025
"I was reading it at lunch and was at the chariot race when lunch ended.

13
00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:02.667
I was dying to know what happened.

14
00:01:02.668 --> 00:01:06.943
So I opened my history book and put Ben-Hur on my lap.

15
00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:09.381
It looked like I was studying history.

16
00:01:09.382 --> 00:01:14.928
I was so interested in it that I never noticed Miss Stacy looking down at me.

17
00:01:14.929 --> 00:01:21.107
I was very ashamed, Marilla, especially when I heard Josie Pye giggling."

18
00:01:21.108 --> 00:01:28.584
Marilla listened with a frown. "Miss Stacy didn't mention that, Anne. It's just your guilty conscience.

19
00:01:28.585 --> 00:01:35.051
Miss Stacy wants to organize a class of students to study for the entrance exam of Queen's College.

20
00:01:35.052 --> 00:01:38.715
She asked Matthew and me if we would like you to join it.

21
00:01:38.716 --> 00:01:42.694
Would you like to go to Queen's College and become a teacher, Anne?"

22
00:01:42.695 --> 00:01:45.824
"Oh, Marilla!" Anne got up from the rug.

23
00:01:45.825 --> 00:01:50.148
"I'd love to be a teacher, but isn't it expensive?"

24
00:01:50.149 --> 00:01:57.055
"Don't worry about that," Marilla said. "Education is important, for girls as much as boys."

25
00:01:57.056 --> 00:02:05.620
"Oh, thank you, Marilla! I'll study as hard as I can, though I warn you not to expect much in geometry," Anne said.

26
00:02:05.621 --> 00:02:14.272
The Queen's class was organized. Gilbert Blythe, Anne Shirley, Ruby Gillis, Josie Pye, and Charlie Sloane joined.

27
00:02:14.273 --> 00:02:19.844
Diana Barry did not, as her parents did not intend to send her to Queen's College.

28
00:02:19.845 --> 00:02:24.535
It was the first time that Diana and Anne had been separated in anything.

29
00:02:24.536 --> 00:02:31.272
When the Queen's class stayed after school for extra lessons, Anne saw Diana leave slowly with the others.

30
00:02:31.273 --> 00:02:37.246
A lump came into Anne's throat, and she hid behind her Latin book to hide the tears in her eyes.

31
00:02:37.247 --> 00:02:42.167
She would never let Gilbert Blythe or Josie Pye see those tears.

32
00:02:42.168 --> 00:02:45.129
Anne enjoyed the Queen's class very much.

33
00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:49.797
She chatted away to Marilla, "Jane and Ruby are studying to be teachers.

34
00:02:49.798 --> 00:02:53.626
Ruby says she'll study for two years and then get married.

35
00:02:53.627 --> 00:03:00.344
Jane says she'll never marry because you are paid for teaching, but a husband won't pay you anything."

36
00:03:00.345 --> 00:03:04.152
"What is Gilbert Blythe going to be?" asked Marilla.

37
00:03:04.153 --> 00:03:09.897
"I don't know what Gilbert's ambition is—if he has one," said Anne scornfully.

38
00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:17.249
Since the day Gilbert had rescued Anne from the bridge and she had not forgiven him, Gilbert had steadily ignored

39
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:21.721
Anne. He talked and joked with the other girls and sometimes walked them

40
00:03:21.722 --> 00:03:27.538
home. But he simply ignored Anne, and Anne found that it was not pleasant to be

41
00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:33.386
ignored. Mrs. Lynde came to Green Gables one afternoon to find out why Marilla had not come to visit

42
00:03:33.387 --> 00:03:38.523
her. "Matthew had chest pains," Marilla explained, "and I thought I shouldn't leave

43
00:03:38.524 --> 00:03:42.961
him. He's all right now, but he gets chest pains more

44
00:03:42.962 --> 00:03:45.983
often. Sit down, Rachel. Will you stay for

45
00:03:45.984 --> 00:03:49.538
tea?" Mrs. Lynde and Marilla ate some biscuits Anne had

46
00:03:49.539 --> 00:03:52.622
made. Mrs. Lynde thought the biscuits were

47
00:03:52.623 --> 00:04:00.292
delicious. "Anne has turned out to be a real smart girl," admitted Mrs. Lynde. "She must be a great

48
00:04:00.293 --> 00:04:05.189
help." "She is," said Marilla, "and she's steady and reliable

49
00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:11.697
too. I was afraid she'd never stop her daydreaming, but she has. I trust her with anything

50
00:04:11.698 --> 00:04:21.516
now." Mrs. Lynde continued, "Yes, she really improved these three years, especially in looks. You could even say she's

51
00:04:21.517 --> 00:04:29.918
pretty." Anne enjoyed her vacation thoroughly. She and Diana spent most of the time outdoors, walking, rowing, and

52
00:04:29.919 --> 00:04:35.074
wandering. When September came, she was ready to study. The Queen's exam

53
00:04:35.075 --> 00:04:39.604
loomed. Anne had a nightmare where she was staring at the pass list for the

54
00:04:39.605 --> 00:04:43.990
exam. Gilbert's name was on top and her name was

55
00:04:43.991 --> 00:04:50.661
absent. The school year passed quickly. Soon June came and the Queen's exams were held in

56
00:04:50.662 --> 00:04:55.090
Charlottetown. "Dearest Diana," wrote Anne in a letter back home to her

57
00:04:55.091 --> 00:05:00.164
friend. "Today we had the history and geometry exam. Geometry was

58
00:05:00.165 --> 00:05:05.392
hard. Josie Pye said the geometry was so easy, a ten-year-old could have done

59
00:05:05.393 --> 00:05:08.847
it. Oh Diana, I wish you were here with

60
00:05:08.848 --> 00:05:14.019
me!" Anne returned to Avonlea and waited for the results to be published in the

61
00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:19.521
newspaper. While she wanted to beat Gilbert Blythe, she also wanted to do well for Matthew and

62
00:05:19.522 --> 00:05:23.375
Marilla—especially Matthew, who said she "would beat the whole island."

63
00:05:23.376 --> 00:05:26.302
That would only happen in her wildest dreams!

64
00:05:26.303 --> 00:05:29.735
But she hoped she would be among the top ten students.

65
00:05:29.736 --> 00:05:35.115
Finally Anne saw Diana racing to Green Gables with a newspaper in her hand.

66
00:05:35.116 --> 00:05:40.558
Anne sprang to her feet. The pass list had been printed! Anne's head whirled.

67
00:05:40.559 --> 00:05:49.699
"Anne, you've passed!" Diana cried. "Passed first—you and Gilbert both. You've tied! Oh, I'm so proud."

68
00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:53.376
Anne grabbed the paper. Yes, she had passed.

69
00:05:53.377 --> 00:05:57.224
There was her name at the very top of a list of two hundred!

70
00:05:57.225 --> 00:06:02.411
That moment was worth living for. Everyone from Avonlea had passed!

71
00:06:02.412 --> 00:06:04.865
They hurried to tell Matthew and Marilla.

72
00:06:04.866 --> 00:06:14.258
"Oh, Matthew," exclaimed Anne, "I've passed and I'm first—or one of the first. I'm not vain, but I'm thankful."

73
00:06:14.259 --> 00:06:19.062
"Well now, I've always said it," said Matthew, gazing at the list happily.

74
00:06:19.063 --> 00:06:21.293
"I knew you could beat them all."

75
00:06:21.294 --> 00:06:36.921
"You've done pretty well, I must say, Anne," said Marilla, trying to hide her extreme pride. "We're all proud of you."

